  "description": "Dependency-free European option pricing, greeks and implied volatility for .NET. Black-Scholes (1973), Merton (1973), Black-76 and Garman-Kohlhagen (1983) as one cost-of-carry-parameterised model. Nine analytic greeks (delta, gamma, vega, theta, two rhos, vanna, volga, charm), Newton-with-bracket implied volatility that reports both convergence and conditioning, market-implied forward and cost-of-carry extraction from call/put pairs, put-call parity, and a double-precision normal distribution accurate to 2.9e-14 relative in both tails. Every greek verified against finite differences, put-call parity and the Black-Scholes PDE identity.",
